=====================================
            ID SELECTOR — NOTES
=====================================

1) The ID selector targets an element by its unique ID.
2) IDs must be UNIQUE — only ONE element should use a specific ID.
3) In CSS, you select an ID using #.
4) IDs are often used for:
   - unique sections
   - specific headings
   - JavaScript targeting
   - single-use styling

Syntax:
#idName {
    property: value;
}

Why IDs must be unique?
- HTML treats an "id" like an identifier.
- It helps browsers, CSS, and JavaScript easily find that one element.
- Using the same ID on multiple elements causes conflicts.

Specificity:
- ID selectors have HIGH specificity.
- They override element selectors and class selectors.

